[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
X-Nemo-Application-Type=silica-qt5
Icon=harbour-pipecam
Name=PipeCam
Comment=USB pipe inspection camera
Comment[de]=USB-Rohrkamera
Exec=harbour-pipecam

# NO [X-Sailjail] SECTION — this is deliberate.
#
# The app opens the camera's raw USB node under /dev/bus/usb/ via libusb (the
# device is vendor-class, so there is no /dev/videoN to request a Camera
# permission for). Sailjail's sandbox gives an application a private /dev with
# only a whitelisted set of nodes, and there is no stock permission that grants
# raw USB access — so a sandboxed build simply cannot reach the camera.
#
# Declaring no [X-Sailjail] section means the app runs unsandboxed, which is the
# same approach harbour-sflipper takes for the Flipper Zero's serial node. The
# trade-off is accepted knowingly: the app has no network code at all, reads
# nothing but the camera, and writes only into ~/Pictures/PipeCam and
# ~/Videos/PipeCam.
